{title: 627 - Jacob's Ladder}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[D/A]We are [Bm]climbing [A]Jacob’s [F#m]ladder,
[Em/G]We are [A]climbing [G]Jacob’s [Bm]ladder,
[D7/C]We [Bm]are climbing [F#m]Jacob’s ladder,
[Em/G]Soldiers [D/F#]ofthe cross.

Verse 2:
[D/A]Every [Bm]round goes [A]higher, [F#m]higher,
[Em/G]Every [A]round [G]goes [Em]higher, [Bm]higher,
[D7/C]Every [Bm]round goes [F#m]higher, higher,
[Em/G]Soldiers of [D/F#]the cross.

Verse 3:
[D/A]Sinner, [Bm]do you [A]love my [F#m]Jesus?
[Em/G]Sinner, [A]do [G]you love [Em]my [Bm]Jesus?
[D7/C]Sinner, [Bm]do you [F#m]love my Jesus?
[Em/G]Soldiers of [D/F#]the cross.

Verse 4:
[D/A]If you [Bm]love him, [A]why not [F#m]serve him?
[Em/G]If you [A]love [G]him, why [Em]not [Bm]serve him?
[D7/C]If [Bm]you love him, [F#m]why not serve [Em/B]him?
[Em/G]Soldiers of [D/F#]the cross.
